<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB3-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB3-003" ;
  triage:title "Exact-match revision resolution refuses every future run past manifest generation" ;
  triage:description "fenix critical review B3, reviewed at 27e21224c. generate_report_index.py:213-225 (resolve_procedures): when source_revision is present, only rev == source_revision is accepted, with no fallback; anything else raises ReportIndexError. The manifest can only hold commits older than the commit that committed it, so every run at any other commit is refused. Reproduced with a synthetic smoke-fast run at 27e21224c: 'procedure smoke-fast has no page for revision 27e21224c' exit 1. run_feature_smoke.py:905-920 write_report -> update_master_report_index() -> SmokeError, so every just smoke <feature> at a non-manifest commit fails at report time; same for colima_skill_report.render and read_benchmark.execute, and for benchmarks. AC4 cannot be met as written. LEAD RULING RECORDED (fenix, design authority for the sprint doc, on PR #1436): D5 rule 1 amended to: exact rev == source_revision if present in the manifest; otherwise the newest manifest entry that is an ancestor of source_revision (git merge-base --is-ancestor <rev> <source_revision>; when git is unavailable, newest entry dated <= generated_at) -- that resolution is exact provenance, not inferred. Date-only resolution (flagged inferred) applies only when source_revision is null. AC4 amended to: a fresh just smoke fast at the PR head links to the newest manifest revision that is an ancestor of its source_revision, without the inferred note. Sprint doc D5/AC4 lines to be updated in the fix commit." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope ".just/generate_report_index.py" ;
  triage:status "fixed_partial" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T19:14:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Routed to cipher's BB3-FIX-R1 alongside the sprint-doc D5/AC4 amendment. Not a schema/DDL change -- resolution-logic and doc text only. BB3-QA2 (req-qa, ATM-QA-013): the ancestor-fallback resolution logic itself (_revision_is_ancestor, .just/generate_report_index.py:204-261) is correct by inspection and the original exact-match-refusal defect is gone, but the fallback path carries zero regression-test coverage in .just/tests/test_generate_report_index.py -- severity downgraded blocking to important to match this residual scope. Routed to cipher's BB3-FIX-R2 (fix/bb3-qa2-r2, per fenix's fix-round-worktree ruling 2026-09-12T20:24:40Z): add a test that exercises _revision_is_ancestor selecting a non-exact ancestor entry." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T19:14:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-003/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

